      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a potential revised intro paragraph:\n\nThe devastating effects of globalization and international trade agreements have led to widespread concerns that nations are ceding control over their economies and workforce to the whims of multinational corporations and global institutions. At its core, the logic of these agreements – which prioritize the elimination of tariffs, quotas, and other protectionist policies in the pursuit of ever-broader global supply chains – appears to be fundamentally at odds with the traditional understanding of national sovereignty. By formally abandoning the right to regulate domestic industries and labor practices, what were once seen as the legitimate tools of statecraft are being effectively ceded to a global, rule-based order that emphasizes economic efficiency and interdependence over national interests. This shift has left many individuals and policymakers wondering whether their government is truly working in their best interests.",
